module coerce_pair.pos_1

// A DECLARED IMPLICIT CONVERSION (E2-b3 wave 5, D429). The pair is DATA read
// from the program -- `#coerce fn str consume @to_bytes() -> Bytes` -- and the
// call site writes nothing: `take("s")` passes a `str` where `Bytes` is
// declared, and the value arrives through the method the program NAMED.
//
// THE EMISSION IS THE NAMED DOOR, and the fixture is built so that a made-up
// conversion could not pass it: `@to_bytes` returns `{ n: 7 }`, a number that
// appears nowhere else in the file, so the printed value is 7 only if THAT
// method ran. A cast, a reinterpretation or a zero-initialised record would
// print something else.
//
// THE `consume` FORM IS THE ORACLE'S RULE, not a preference: D429 R2 gives the
// non-`consume` (view) lane the obligation to return `ro O`, and the oracle
// refuses the shape that does not (measured 2026-08-23, which is how this
// fixture came to be written the other way round).
type Bytes { n int }

#coerce fn str consume @to_bytes() -> Bytes => { n: 7 }

fn take(b Bytes) -> int => b.n

fn main() {
    println(take("s"))
}
